sections.body_md:
Walk round the boundary and add every piece:
- sector: arc $+ 2r$;
- segment: arc $+$ chord;
- a quadrant-cornered park edge: straight parts $+$ arcs (four quadrant arcs $= 2\pi r$);
- a ring track: the outer edge exceeds the inner edge by $2\pi \times$ width.

*Example:* quadrant of radius $14$ cm: arc $22$ cm, perimeter $50$ cm; $90^\circ$ segment of radius $14$ cm: $22 + 14\sqrt2 \approx 41.80$ cm.

questions.stem_md:
A chord $AB$ of a circle with centre $O$ and radius $21$ cm subtends $60^\circ$ at $O$. Find:

(a) the length of the minor arc $AB$;

(b) the area of the minor sector $OAB$;

(c) the area of the minor segment;

(d) the area of the major segment.
Use $\pi = \dfrac{22}{7}$ and $\sqrt3 = 1.73$.
